  "caveats": [
    "DECODING: reasoning disabled at the provider key level for every model and both arms, identically, as in L1 and L2. This measures direct legibility without a deliberation subsidy.",
    "SCALE: development experiment -- 3 tasks, 11 questions, N=3, 33 paired cells per model per arm, 132 pooled per arm. A development signal, not a significance test. Its force comes from the failure being one axis in four independent families, and from agreeing with L1 and L2.",
    "PROVIDER IDENTITY: routing identity verified by the qualified boundary (requested == reported on every attempt, no substitution), but underlying community-hosted weights were not independently attested; model self-identification was inconsistent across runs and is treated as non-authoritative output. A limit of provider identity assurance, not a substitution failure.",
    "PROMPT NEUTRALITY: both arms used identical scaffolding with neither representation named and no reading tutorial for either, so RAW was re-run fresh rather than inherited from L1/L2. The token accounting was recomputed from the final prompts (10.92%), not carried over from L3A (9.61%).",
    "STRUCTURAL: jstruct is byte-lossless (exact roundtrip verified through the real decoder on all three contexts before any call). The difference measured is comprehension, not fidelity."
  ],
  "finding": "Removing the dictionary entirely did not remove the reading cost. jstruct is byte-lossless, carries no legend, keeps every identifier literal, needs no notation block, and saves 10.92% cold -- and still no model reached non-inferiority. Pooled correctness fell 70 -> 66 and the only axis that moved against it is missing_required_witness (60 -> 65); all 13 paired hard regressions, across all four families, are that same axis. Taken with L1 (aliasing corrupts references and costs thoroughness) and L2 (protecting identifiers removes the corruption but not the thoroughness cost), the boundary is now located: for this evidence-heavy JSON workload, restructuring the context at all -- even into a legible, literal, dictionary-free table -- costs the model evidence it would otherwise have cited. The JSON structure is itself part of the reading interface.",
